hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1156","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Hajjaj, Ibn Jurayj said: Abdullah bin Musafa’ told me that Mus’ab bin Shaybah told him, on the authority of Utbah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Ja`far, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever doubts In his prayer, let him prostrate two prostrations after the salutation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1157","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Hajjaj and Ruh, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Abdullah bin Musafa’ told me that Mus’ab bin Shaybah told him, on the authority of Utbah bin Muhammad bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jafar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is in doubt about a prayer, let him prostrate two prostrations.” Hajjaj said: “After he has said the salutation,” and a spirit said: “While he is sitting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1158","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “When one of you stands up to pray, Satan comes to him and overwhelms him to the point that he does not know how many times he has prayed. So if one of you finds that, Let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting.”"
"1159","Bishr bin Hilal told us, he said: Abd al-Warith, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When prayer is called, Satan will prepare for his farts, and when the yawning is finished, It approaches until it comes to a person’s heart that he does not know how long he has prayed, so if one of you sees that, let him prostrate two prostrations.”"
"1160","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, and the wording is by Ibn Al-Muthanna. He said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the noon prayer five times,” so it was said to him: What should be added to the prayer? He said: “What is that?” They said: You prayed five times, so he bent his leg and prostrated two times. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1161","Abdah bin Abd al-Rahim told me. He said: I am Ibn Shumail. He said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah. On the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he led them in the noon prayer five times, and they said: “You prayed five times.” So he prostrated two prostrations. After he had greeted him, while he was sitting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1162","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, from Yahya bin Adam, he said: from Mufaddal, and he is Ibn Muhalhal, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim Ibn Suwayd, he said: Alqamah prayed five times, then he was told, and he said: What did you do? So I said with my head: Yes, he said: And you, one-eyed? So I said: Yes, so he prostrated two prostrations, then he told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he prayed five times, and some The people turned to one another, so they said to him: Should I add more prayer? He said: “No.” So they told him, so he bent his legs and prostrated twice, then he said: “I am only a human being. I forget as you forget.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1163","Suwayd, I am Abdullah, told us on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Alqamah prayed five times, and when he said the salaam, he said: Ibrahim bin Suwayd: O Abu Shibl, you prayed five times. He said: Is that the case, O one-eyed man? “So he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, and said: This is what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did.”"
"1164","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Nahshali, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed one of the evening prayers as five times, and it was said to him: Should I add more prayers? He said: “What is that?” They said: I prayed five times. He said: “I am only a human being. I forget as you forget, and I remember as you remember.” So he prostrated twice. Then it twisted"
"1165","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf, a servant Uthman, on the authority of his father Yusuf, that Muawiyah prayed in front of them, so he stood up during the prayer and had a seat on him, so the people praised him, so he continued to stand, then he prostrated with us. He prostrated two times while he was sitting after he had completed the prayer, then he sat on the pulpit and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Whoever forgets something of his prayer, let him prostrate before these two prostrations.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1166","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh Abu Al-Tahir told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr, Yunus, and Al-Layth told me that Ibn Shihab told them, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, that Abd Allah ibn Buhaynah told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose in At two o'clock in the afternoon, he did not sit, so when he finished his prayer, he prostrated two prostrations, saying the takbir in each prostration while he was sitting, before he said the salutation. And the people prostrated them with him, in the place where he had forgotten to sit.”"
"1167","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi and Muhammad bin Bashar Bundar told us, and the pronunciation is his. He said: Na Yahya bin Saeed. He said: Na Abd. Al-Hamid bin Jaafar, he said: Muhammad bin Ata’ told me, on the authority of Abu Humaid Al-Sa’idi, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to: “If he was in The two rak'ahs in which the prayer ends, he lowered his left leg and sat on his side, bowing, then said the salaam. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1168","Qutaibah informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Hajar, he said: “I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he raises his hands when he begins the prayer, and when he bows, and when he raises his head from bowing, and when he sits, he makes the left one lie down, and he puts the right one in the position of the right. He placed his left hand on his left thigh, and his right hand on his right thigh, and held two hands: the middle and the thumb, and indicated with the index finger\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1169","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Maymun al-Ruqi told me, he said: we were told by Muhammad, and he is the son of Yusuf al-Faryabi, he said: we were told by Sufyan, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Wael bin Hajar, that he saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He sat in prayer, spread out his left leg, and placed his arms on his thighs, and pointed with his index finger, supplicating. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1170","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr bin al-Mufaddal told us, he said: Asim bin Kulayb told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wael bin Hajar, he said: I said: Let us see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, how he prays. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up, faced the Qiblah, and raised He raised his hands until they were in line with his ears, then he took his left hand with his right. When he wanted to bow, he raised them like that, and placed his hands on the His knees, and when he raised his head from bowing, he raised them in the same way. Then, when he prostrated, he placed his head on that place from his hands, then he sat. So he spread his left leg, put his left hand on his left thigh, and placed his right elbow on his right thigh, and made two fists. “And he flew, and I saw him saying like this, and Bishr pointed with his right index finger, and he flew with his thumb and middle.”"
"1171","Muhammad bin Mansour, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, informed us on the authority of Muslim bin Abi Maryam, a sheikh from the people of Medina. Then I met The Sheikh, and he said: I heard Ali bin Abdul Rahman say: I prayed next to Ibn Umar, and I stirred up the pebbles, and Ibn Umar said to me, “Do not stir up the pebbles.” Turning over pebbles is from the devil, and do as you saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing. I said: How did you see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He, peace and blessings be upon him, does this? He said: “Thus” and he put the right one up, and he put the left one down, and put his right hand on his right thigh, and his left hand on his thigh. left hand, and pointed with his index finger.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1172","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Muslim bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Ali bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Ibn Umar saw me while I was I was playing with pebbles during prayer, and when he left, he forbade me and said: Do as it was, meaning the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, does. I said: How? was he making? He said: “When he sat in prayer, he would place his right palm on his thigh, clench all his fingers, and point with the finger next to the thumb. And he placed his left palm on his left thigh.”"
"1173","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Zaida, he said: Asim bin Kulayb told us, he said: My father told me that Wael bin Hajar said: I said: Let us look at the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, how he prays? So I looked at him, and he described. He said: Then he sat down, spread out his left leg, and placed his left palm on his thigh and his left knee. He placed the edge of his right elbow on his right thigh, then he closed two of his fingers and circled them, then he raised his finger and I saw him move them. He calls upon it, brief.”"
"1174","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, on the authority of Abdul Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “When he sat in prayer, he would place his hands on his knees, and raise the finger next to the thumb to pray with it, and his left hand would be on his knee.” He spread it out over her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1175","Ayoub bin Muhammad al-Wazzan told me, Hajjaj told us, Ibn Jurayj said: Ziyad told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Aamir bin Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He used to point with his finger when he called and would not move it,” he said. Ibn Jurayj, and Amr added, saying: Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair told me, on the authority of his father, that he saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He prays like this, and supports himself with his left hand, on his left leg. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1176","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar Al-Mawsili told me, on the authority of Al-Mu’afia, on the authority of Issam bin Qudamah, on the authority of Malik, who is Ibn Numayr. Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of his father, said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, placing his right hand on his right thigh during prayer, indicating With his finger (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1177","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Safwan told us, he said: Ibn Ajlan told us, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that A man was praying with his two fingers, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “One, one.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1178","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Saad, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by me. May God bless him and grant him peace, and I was supplicating with my fingers. He said: “Ahad Ahad” and pointed with his index finger. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1179","Ahmad bin Yahya Al-Sufi told us, from Abu Nu’aym, he said: Issam bin Qudamah Al-Jadli told me, Malik bin Numayr Al-Khuza’i told me, from The people of Basra, that his father told him that he saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “sitting in prayer, placing his right arm on His right thigh, raising his index finger, bent it slightly while he was supplicating.”"
"1180","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, Yahya told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Amir bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “When he sat for the tashahhud, he would place his left palm on his left thigh, and point with his index finger, not going beyond his sight.” \his signal\"""""""
"1181","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, al-Layth informed me, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Rabi’ah, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Some people will refrain from raising their eyes when supplicating in prayer until heaven, or their eyes will be snatched away.”"
"1182","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Abu Ubaid Allah Al-Makhzoumi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, and Mansour, on the authority of Shaqiq ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: We used to say in prayer, before the tashahhud was made obligatory: Peace be upon God, peace be upon Gabriel, and Michael, so the Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Do not say like this, for God is peace, but say: “Greetings are to God, and prayers and good things, peace be upon you.” O Prophet, God’s mercy and blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant. and His Messenger\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1183","Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Humaid told us, Abu al-Zubair told us, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to teach us the Tashahhud, just as he taught us a surah from the Qur’an.”"
"1184","Qutaybah told us, this is Al-Fudayl Ibn Iyad, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Indeed, God is peace, so when one of you sits, let him say: Greetings are to God, and prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet.” By God’s mercy and blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Then he may choose to speak after whatever he wants.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1185","Muhammad bin Bashar bin Kaysan Bundar told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Qatada, and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Yunus ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Hattan ibn Abdullah, that Al-Ash’ari said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us, taught us our Sunnah, and explained to us our prayer. He said: “When you stand up to pray, straighten your rows, then Let one of you lead you in prayer. When he says “Allahu Akbar,” say “Allahu Akbar,” then when he says: “Not even those who go astray,” then say: “Ameen,” God will answer you. Then when he says “Allahu Akbar” and bows, So say “Allahu Akbar” and bow, for the Imam is bowing before you.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So do that with that, and when he says: God hears To whoever praises Him, say: Oh God, our Lord, praise be to You, for God said on the tongue of His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: God hears those who praise Him, then When he says “Allahu Akbar” and prostrates, “Allahu Akbar” and prostrate, for the Imam prostrates before you, and rises before you.” The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ And if it is while sitting, let it be the saying of one of you to say: Good greetings and prayers are for God, peace be upon you. O Prophet, God’s mercy and blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is His servant. and His Messenger\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1186","Amr bin Ali told us, Abu Asim told us, Ayman bin Nabul told us, he said: Abu Al-Zubayr told us, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, teaches us the Tashahhud, just as he teaches us the surah from the Qur’an: “In the name of God and by God, greetings are to God, and prayers and good deeds, peace.” Upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. I ask God for Paradise, and I seek refuge in God from Hell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1187","Abd al-Wahhab bin Abd al-Hakam al-Warraq told me, he said: I am Muadh bin Muadh, on the authority of Sufyan bin Saeed, and Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, He said: Waki’ and Abd al-Razzaq, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, to God are angels who are traveling, who convey to me peace from my nation.”"
"1188","Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Kawsaj Al-Maruzi told us: I am Affan, he is Hammad, I am Thabit. He said: Sulayman, the servant of Al-Hasan bin Ali, at the time of Al-Hajjaj, told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came one day And the good news is on his face, so we said, “Indeed, we will see the good news on your face.” He said: “The angel came to me and said: O Muhammad, indeed your Lord says: Would you not be satisfied with the fact that no one prays upon you except that I have prayed for him ten times, and no one greets you except that I have greeted him ten times?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1189","Muhammad bin Salamah, narrated by Ibn Wahb, told us, on the authority of Haywa bin Shurayh, on the authority of Abu Hani, that Abu Ali al-Janabi told him, that He heard Fadalah bin Ubaid say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a man calling in prayer who did not glorify God and did not pray for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You haveten, O praying person.” Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, taught them, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, heard them. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a man praying, so he glorified God and praised Him, and sent blessings upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: “Call and it will be answered, ask and it will be given to you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1190","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, a reading of it, and I am listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Naim bin Abdullah Al-Mujmar, that Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Zaid Al-Ansari, and Abdullah bin Zaid, who was shown The call to prayer. He told him, on the authority of Abu Masoud Al-Ansari, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us in the gathering of Saad bin Worship, so Bashir bin Saad said to him: God has commanded us to pray for you, O Messenger of God, so how can we pray for you? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was silent until we wished he had not asked him, then he said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You have blessed the family of Abraham, and you have blessed Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, just as you have blessed the family of Abraham in the worlds. You are Praiseworthy and Glorious, and peace, as you have \You knew\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1191","Ziyad bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Abdul Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed, he said: On the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Bishr, on the authority of Abu Masoud Al-Ansari, who said: It was said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: We were commanded to pray upon you and to greet you, but as for peace, it was We knew him, so how can we pray for you? He said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad, as You blessed Abraham’s family. O God, bless Muhammad’s family, as You blessed Abraham’s family.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1192","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, from his book, he said: Husayn bin Ali, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah On the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ka`b ibn Ujrah, he said: We said, O Messenger of God: We have known peace be upon you, so how is the prayer? He said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed the family of Abraham. You are Praiseworthy and Glorious. O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, just as You blessed the family of Abraham, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” And Ibn Abi Laila said: And we say, “And upon us is with them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1193","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ka’b bin Ujrah, who said: We said: O Messenger of God, peace be upon you. We have known it, so how can we pray for you? He said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Abraham and the family of Abraham. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious, and bless Muhammad, and upon the family of Muhammad, just as You blessed Abraham and Abraham’s family. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” Abdul Rahman said: And we say: And upon us. With them, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This one is more correct than the one before it. We do not know of anyone who said about it: Amr ibn Murrah other than this one. He is famous for his wisdom (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1194","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, he said: Ka’b bin Ujrah said to me: Don’t Shall I give you a gift? We said: O Messenger of God, we know how to greet you, so how do we pray for you? He said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed the family of Abraham. You are Praiseworthy and Glorious. O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad.” Just as You blessed the family of Abraham, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1195","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Bishr, he said: Ours is Muja’ bin Yahya, on the authority of Uthman bin Muhib, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of his father, said: We said, O Messenger of God, how is the prayer upon you? He said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad, as You blessed Abraham and the family of Abraham. You are Praiseworthy and Glorious, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad.” Just as You blessed Abraham and the family of Abraham, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1196","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: We are my uncle, he said: We are a partner, on the authority of Uthman bin Mawhib, on the authority of Musa bin Talha On the authority of his father, that a man came to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: How can we pray for you, O Prophet of God? He said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad, as You blessed Abraham, for You are Praiseworthy and Glorious, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, just as You blessed Abraham, you are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1197","Saeed bin Yahya bin Saeed the Umayyad told us, in his hadith, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uthman bin Hakim, on the authority of Khaled bin Salamah, on the authority of Musa Ibn Talha, he said: I asked Zayd Ibn Kharijah, he said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Pray for me, and strive to Supplication, and say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1198","Qutaibah bin Saeed, our descendant Bakr, who is Ibn Mudar, told us on the authority of Ibn al-Haad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Khabab, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: We said, O Messenger of God: We have known this greeting upon you, so how can we pray upon you? He said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, as You blessed Abraham, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Abraham (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1199","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, a reading of it, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym al-Zarqi, who said: Abu Hamid Al-Saadi told me that they said: O Messenger of God, how can we pray for you? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad, his wives, and his offspring” in the hadith of Al-Harith, “just as you bless The family of Abraham, and bless Muhammad, his wives, and his descendants.” They all said: “Just as You blessed the family of Abraham, for You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” Qutaibah told us about this hadith twice, and perhaps a line of it was dropped from him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1200","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, I am Abdullah, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, I am Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Suleiman, the client of Al-Hasan bin Ali, On the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came one day while people could see his face, and he said “Indeed, Gabriel came to me and said: Indeed, your Lord says: Would it not please you, O Muhammad, that no one of your nation prays upon you except that I pray upon him ten times?” “And no one from your nation will greet you except that I will greet him ten times.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1201","Ali bin Hajar, our son Ismail, who is the son of Jafar, told us on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever prays one prayer for me, may God bless him ten times.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1202","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Yusuf, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, we told Anas bin Malik He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays one prayer over me, God will send ten prayers over him, and ten sins will be removed from him.” And he was raised ten degrees.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1203","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi and Amr bin Ali told us, and the wording for it, they said: Yahya told us, he said: Sulaiman, who is Al-Amash, told us: A brother told me, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: When we sat with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in prayer, we would say: Peace be upon God from His servants. Peace be upon so-and-so and so-and-so. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not say: Peace be upon God, for God is peace. But if one of you sits, Let him say: Greetings are to God, and prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the servants of God. The righteous, for if you say that, it will apply to every righteous servant in heaven and earth. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad His servant and Messenger, then let him choose a supplication after he liked it and supplicate with it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1204","Ubaid bin Wakee’ bin Al-Jarrah told me, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, On the authority of Anas, he said: Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, teach me words that I can use in my prayer. He said: “Glorify God ten times, praise Him ten times, glorify Him ten times, then ask Him for your need.” He says: “Yes, yes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1205","Qutaibah told us, he said: We are Khalaf, meaning Ibn Khalifa, on the authority of Hafs, the son of my brother Anas, on the authority of Anas, he said: I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him, sitting, meaning, with a man standing and praying, so when he kneeled, prostrated, and recited the tashahhud, he supplicated, and said in his supplication: “O God, I ask you, that Praise be to You, there is no god but You, Al-Mannan, Creator of the heavens and the earth, O Possessor of majesty and honor, O Ever-Living, O Sustaining One. Indeed, I ask of You, and he said The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to his companions: “Do you know what he called for?” They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, he has called upon His Great Name, which when called upon by it, responds. He was asked with it, he was given.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1206","Amr ibn Yazid al-Basri Abu Buraid informed us, on the authority of Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith, he said: My father told us, Husayn told us, meaning the teacher, On the authority of Ibn Buraidah, Hanzalah bin Ali narrated to me, that Muhjan bin Al-Adra’ narrated to him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque When a man prayed while reciting the tashahhud, he said: Oh God, I ask you, O God, the One, the Only, the Eternal, the One who does not beget, nor was born, nor was He is equal to anyone. Please forgive me my sins. Indeed, You are the Forgiving, the Merciful. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He has been forgiven” three times."
"1207","Qutaibah told us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, He said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Teach me a supplication that I will pray with in my prayers. He said: “Say: Oh God, I have wronged myself greatly, and do not “No one forgives sins except You, so grant me forgiveness from You, and have mercy on me. Indeed, You are the Forgiving, the Merciful.”"
"1208","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, he said: I heard Haywa speaking, on the authority of Uqba bin Muslim, on the authority of Abu Abdul-Rahman. Al-Hubli, on the authority of Al-Sanabihi, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took my hand and said: “I love you, O Muadh.” So I said: And I love you, O Messenger of God. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So do not neglect saying in every prayer: My Lord, help me in remembering You. And thank you, and worship you well.”"
"1209","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Sulayman narrated to us, meaning bin Harb, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Shaddad Ibn Aws, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in his prayer: “O God, I ask you for steadfastness in the matter and determination to follow the right path. And I ask You to be grateful for Your blessings, and to worship You well, and I ask You for a sound heart and a sincere tongue, and I ask You for the best of what You know, and I seek refuge in protect you from the evil of what you know, and I ask forgiveness from you for what you know.”"
"1210","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi, narrated to us by Hammad, narrated to us by Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, said: Ammar bin Yasir led a prayer for us, So he explained it briefly, and some people said to him: You have shortened or shortened the prayer, so he said: As for that, I prayed to God about it. With invitations that I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he got up, a man from the people, who was my father, followed him, but he concealed his himself, so he asked him about the supplication, then he came and told the people about it: “O God, with your knowledge of the unseen, and your ability to create, keep me alive as long as you know Life is good for me, and cause me to die if You know that death is good for me. O God, I ask You to fear You, meaning in the unseen and witnessed, and I ask You to fear You. A word of wisdom in contentment and anger, and I ask you for wisdom in poverty and wealth, and I ask you for a bliss that does not fade away, and I ask you for the comfort of an eye that does not You will be cut off, and I ask you for satisfaction after you have made it up, and I ask you for the joy of life after death, and I ask you for the pleasure of looking at your face. And the longing to meet You, without harmful adversity or misleading temptation. O God, adorn us with the adornment of faith, and make us rightly guided.”"
"1211","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: We are my uncle, he said: We are a partner, on the authority of Abu Hashim al-Wasiti, on the authority of Abu Majliz On the authority of Qais bin Abbad, he said: Ammar bin Yasser led the people with a prayer that he concealed, as if they had denied it. He said: Did I not complete the bowing and prostration? They said: Yes, he said: As for me, I prayed with it a supplication that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray with: “O God, with your knowledge of the unseen and your ability to Creation, keep me alive as long as You know that life is good for me, and cause me to die when You know that death is good for me, and I ask You for Your fear in the unseen and the witnessed. And the word sincerity in contentment and anger, and I ask you for endless bliss, and the comfort of an eye that never ceases, and I ask you to be content with your decree, and coolness. Life after death, the pleasure of looking at your face, and the longing to meet you, and I seek refuge in you from harmful adversity and misleading trials, O God. “Adorn us with the adornment of faith and make us guides.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1212","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, I am Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Farwa bin Nawfal, he said: I said to Aisha, Tell me something. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to call for it in his prayers. She said: Yes. He used to say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of What I did, and from the evil of what I did not do.”"
"1213","Muhammad ibn Bashar informed us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Shu’bah, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I asked The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the torment of the grave, and he said: “Yes, the torment of the grave is real.” Aisha said: I did not see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, he will pray one prayer after that, unless he seeks refuge from the torment of the grave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1214","Amr bin Uthman told me, my father told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Urwa told me that Aisha told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray during prayer: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the temptation of the Antichrist. And I seek refuge in You from the trials of life and death. Oh God, I seek refuge in You from sin and debt. Someone said: How often do you seek refuge? Who is in love? He said: “When a man is in debt, he tells a lie, makes a promise, then breaks it.”"
"1215","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Mu’afah, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, and I am Ali bin Khashram, on the authority of Issa bin Yunus, and the pronunciation for him, On the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan, he is Ibn Atiyya, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abi Aisha, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “When one of you bears witness, let him seek refuge from four things: from the torment of Hell, the torment of the grave, and the temptation of life.” And death, and from the evil of the Antichrist. Then he will pray for himself according to what appears to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1216","Amr ibn Ali, narrated to us by Yahya, on the authority of Ja`far, who is the son of Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to say in his prayer after the Tashahhud: “The best speech is the speech of God, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1217","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Adam, he said: On the authority of Malik, and he is Ibn Mughal, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Zaid bin Wahb, on the authority of Hudhayfah, said that he saw a man praying, so he became humble, and Hudhayfah said to him: How long have you been praying this prayer? He said: Forty years ago. He said: “You have not prayed for forty years, and if you died praying this prayer, you would have died other than the nature of Muhammad, peace be upon him.” Prayers and peace, then he said: “The man will lighten his prayers, complete his prayers, and do good.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1218","Qutaybah, on the authority of Al-Layth, informed us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Ali ibn Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of an uncle of his, Badri, that he narrated to him, A man entered the mosque and prayed, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at him, and we were not aware. When he finished, he came and greeted the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” So he went back and prayed, then he went to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted him and said: “Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” two or three times, so the man said to him: By the one who honored you, O Messenger of God, you have worked hard. So he taught me, and said: “When you stand up intending to pray, perform ablution, do your ablution well, then face the Qiblah, say the takbir, then recite, then Kneel down, and be at ease while kneeling, then rise until you are upright standing, then prostrate until you are at ease prostrating, then rise until you are at ease sitting, then Prostrate until you are secure in your prostration, then rise, then do so until you have finished your prayer.”"
"1219","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, told us on the authority of Dawud bin Qais, he said: Ali bin Yahya bin told me. Khalad bin Rafi’ bin Malik Al-Ansari said: My father told me, on the authority of an uncle, Badri, who said: I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was sitting in the mosque, and a man entered and prayed two rak’ahs, then he came and greeted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He greeted him while he was praying, and he returned his greetings, then said to him: “Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” So he returned and prayed, then he came and greeted Ali. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, returned his greetings, then said to him: “Go back and pray, for you have not prayed,” until it was the third or fourth hour. He said: By the One who sent down the Book to you, I have striven and been careful, so show me and teach me. He said: “If you want to pray, perform ablution, and do well.” Your ablution, then face the Qiblah, then say “Allahu Akbar”, then recite, then bow until you are at ease in your bowing, then rise until you stand up straight, then Prostrate until you are at ease prostrate, then rise until you are at ease sitting, then prostrate until you are at ease prostrate, then rise, and when you have completed Your prayer for this has been completed, and whatever you detract from this, you are only detracting from your prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1220","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, he said: I said: Oh Mother of the Believers, tell me about the Witr prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: “We used to prepare for him his siwak and to purify him, so he would send him When God willed, He would raise him up in the middle of the night, so he would use himself and perform ablution, pray eight rak’ahs, and would not sit in them except at the eighth, then he would sit Then he remembers God and supplicates, then he greets us with complete salutation, making us hear.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1221","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, Sulaiman bin Daoud Al-Hashimi told us, Ibrahim, who is Ibn Saad, told me. Abdullah bin Jafar means Al-Mukhrami, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad, Aamir bin Saad told me, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He salutes to his right and to his left.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1222","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, I am Abu Amir Al-Aqdi, we are Abdullah bin Jaafar, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of Amer Ibn Saad, on the authority of Saad, said: “I used to see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeting him to his right and to his left until the white of his cheek could be seen.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1223","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin al-Qibtiyyah, he said: I heard Jabir bin Samra, He said: When we prayed behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, we would say: Peace be upon you, peace be upon you, and Mas’ar pointed with his hand, to his right and to the To his left, he said: “What is the matter with these who throw their hands as if they were the tails of sun-horses?! Isn’t it enough for one of them to put his hand on So his thigh, then he greets his brother, to his right and to his left.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1224","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Muadh ibn Muadh, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of al-Aswad, And Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying ‘Allahu Akbar’ in every lowering, raising, standing and sitting, and saying salaam on the authority of To his right and to his left: “Peace, mercy, and blessings of God be upon you, peace and mercy of God be upon you,” until the white of his cheek could be seen. “And I saw Abu Bakr And Omar, they do that (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1225","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani told us, Hajjaj, Ibn Jurayj said, I am Amr bin Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of His uncle, Wasi bin Hibban, said that he asked Abdullah bin Omar about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “God is great” whenever He placed, “Allahu Akbar,” whenever he raised it, then he said, “Peace and God’s mercy be upon you,” on his right. “Peace and God’s mercy be upon you,” on his left. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1226","Qutaibah told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Amr ibn Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, on the authority of his uncle Wasi ibn Hibban, He said: I said to Ibn Umar: Tell me about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. How was it? He said: He mentioned the takbeer, meaning, and he mentioned: “Peace and mercy of God be upon you” on his right, and “Peace and mercy of God be upon you” on his left. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1227","Zayd bin Akhzam told me, on the authority of Ibn Dawud, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is as if I am looking at the white of his cheek. On his right: “Peace and God’s mercy be upon you,” and on his left: “Peace.” May God’s mercy be upon you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1228","Muhammad bin Adam told me, on the authority of Omar bin Ubaid, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, he greets on his right, until the white of his cheek is visible, and on his left, until the white of his cheek is visible.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1229","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: It is Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: He used to salute to his right and to his left: “Peace and mercy of God be upon you, peace be upon you and God’s mercy” until he could see “The white of his cheek is on this side, and the white of his cheek is on that side.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1230","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq told me, he said: Al-Hussein bin Waqid told me, he said: Abu Ishaq told me, on the authority of Alqamah, And Al-Aswad, and Abu Al-Ahwas, they said: We are Abdullah bin Masoud, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “salutate on his right”: “peace be upon him.” May God’s mercy and blessings be upon you” until the white of his right cheek can be seen, and on his left: “May the peace and mercy of God be upon you” until the white of his left cheek can be seen."
"1231","Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Na Israel, on the authority of Furat al-Qazzaz, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, who is Ibn al-Qibtiyyah, On the authority of Jabir bin Samurah, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when we greeted us, we would say with our hands: Peace be upon you, peace be upon you. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at us and said: “What is the matter with you, pointing with your hands as if they were the tails of sunken horses? When he greeted us, One of you, let him turn to his friend and not gesture with his hand.”"
"1232","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, I am Abdullah and he is Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he told him, he said: Mahmoud informed me Al-Rabi’ bin Al-Rabi’ said: I heard Itban bin Malik saying: I was praying for my people, Banu Salem, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: : I have denied my sight, and the floods prevent me from the mosque of my people, so I wished that you would come, and prayed in my house, a place that I could take. prostrating, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I will do so, God willing.” So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Abu Bakr came to me tomorrow. After the day became intense, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, asked for permission, and I gave him permission, but he did not sit until he said: “Where would you like me to pray from?” “Your house?” So I pointed to him the place where he liked to pray. “So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and we lined up behind him, then he greeted us.” And he greeted us when he greeted us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1233","Suleiman bin Dawud bin Hammad bin Saad, the son of my brother Rishdin bin Saad Abu Al-Rabi’, informed us on the authority of Ibn Wahb. He said: Ibn Abu Dhib, Amr bin Al-Harith, and Yunus, that Ibn Shihab told them, on the authority of Urwa, Aisha said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace, he prays eleven rak’ahs between the end of the evening prayer and the dawn prayer, and he performs Witr with one rak’ah, and prostrates prostration as much as one of you recites fifty verses before raising his head.” And some of them exceed others in hadith, brief."
"1234","Muhammad ibn Adam informed me, on the authority of Hafs, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace “He greeted, then spoke, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1235","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, I am Abdullah, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, he said: I am Damdam bin Jus, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He said the salutations, then he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, while he was sitting, then he saluted,” he said: He mentioned it in the hadith of Dhul-Yadin."
"1236","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed three times, then gave the salutation, and Al-Khirbaq said: You prayed three times, so he prayed the remaining rak’ah with them, then “ He said the salaam, then he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then he said the salaam.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1237","Ahmad ibn Sulayman informed us, on the authority of Amr ibn Aoun, on the authority of Abu Awanah, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of al-Bara’ Ibn Aazib, who said: “I looked at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying, and I found him standing, and I bowed, and he stood up straight after the rak’ah. So I prostrated him, and made him sit between the two prostrations, so I prostrated him, and made him sit, between the salutation and the departure, close to the same.”"
"1238","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Yunus. Ibn Shihab said: Hind bint al-Harith al-Farasiyya told me that Umm Salamah I told her: “The women during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would stand up when they finished praying, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood firm.” And whoever of the men prayed as God willed, then when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up, the men would stand up.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1239","Ya'qub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Sufyan, Ya'la bin Ata told me, on the authority of Jabir bin Yazid bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of His father: “He prayed the morning prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but when he prayed, he deviated.”"
"1240","Bishr bin Khaled Al-Askari told us, I am Yahya bin Adam, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Ma’bad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “I only knew that the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ended with the takbeer.”"
"1241","Muhammad ibn Salamah told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Hunayn ibn Abi Hakim, on the authority of Ali ibn Rabah, on the authority of Uqba ibn Amer said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to recite the Mu’awwidhat after every prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1242","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Abu Amr, meaning Al-Awza’i, he said: Shaddad Abu Ammar told me that Abu Asma Al-Rahbi told him that he heard Thawban, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was... He left his prayer, asked for forgiveness three times, and said: “O God, You are peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of majesty and honor.”"
"1243","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala and Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Sadran told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would say: “O God, you are the peace, and from you is peace. Blessed are you.” Possessor of majesty and honor.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1244","Muhammad ibn Shuja’ al-Marwadhi told me, Ismail told me, on the authority of al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman, he said: Abu al-Zubayr told me, I heard Abdullah Ibn al-Zubayr, speaking on this pulpit, and he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say the salutation: “There is no god but God.” He alone has no partner, to Him belongs dominion, to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things, and there is no power or strength except in God, there is no god but God, and there is no We worship none but Him, the people of grace, grace, and good praise, there is no god but God, sincere in religion to Him, even if the disbelievers hate it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1245","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am a slave, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, he said: He was Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr. He exclaims at the end of the prayer, saying: “There is no god but Allah, He alone has no partner, to Him belongs dominion, and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. There is no god but “Allah, and we worship none but Him. To Him is grace, and to Him is favour, and to Him is good praise. There is no god but Allah, sincere in religion to Him, even if the disbelievers hate it.” Then Ibn al-Zubayr says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to greet them at the end of prayer."
"1246","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: I heard it from Abdah bin Abi Lubabah, and I heard it from Abd al-Malik, both of them They heard from Wardad, the scribe of Al-Mughira ibn Shu’bah, who said: Mu’awiyah wrote to Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, telling me something I heard from the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would complete the prayer, he would say: “There is no god but God alone, without any partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things. O God, there is no hinderer of what You have given, nor giver of what You have withheld, and the grandfather does not benefit from you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1247","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Musayyab Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of Ward, who said: Al-Mughirah wrote to Muawiyah: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say after the prayer when he said the salutation: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise.” And He is Able to do all things. O God, there is no one who prevents what You have given, and there is no giver of what You withhold, and no one who is serious can benefit from you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1248","Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Suleiman Al-Mujalidi told us, he said: I am Hushaym, I am Mughirah, and he mentioned the end of it, and Yaqoub bin Ibrahim, he said: Na Hushaym, I am not one of them. Mugheerah, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Ward, the writer of Al-Mugheerah ibn Shu’bah, that Muawiyah wrote To Al-Mughirah to write to me about a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Al-Mughirah wrote to him: I heard him say when... His departure from prayer: “There is no god but Allah, He alone has no partner, to Him belongs dominion, and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things” three times."
"1249","Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Salama Al-Khuza’i, Mansur bin Salamah, Khallad bin Suleiman, Abu Salamah said, and he was one of the The fearful, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Imran, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat, Or he prayed, he spoke some words, then Aisha asked him about the words, and he said: “If he speaks well, he will be in charge of them until the Day of Resurrection. And if he spoke otherwise than that, it would be an expiation for him: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1250","Ahmad ibn Sulaiman, narrated to us by Ya’la, narrated by Qudamah, informed us on the authority of Jasra, she said: Aisha narrated to me, she said: A woman from The Jews, and she said: The torment of the grave is due to urine, so I said: You lied, and she said: Yes, indeed, indeed, We will remove from it the skin and the garment. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to pray, and our voices rose, so he said: “What is this?!” So I told him what she said, He said: “You have spoken the truth.” He did not pray after that day except that he said at the end of the prayer: “O Lord of Gabriel, Michael, and Israfil, protect me from the heat of the Fire. And the torment of the grave.”"
"1251","Amr bin Sawad bin Al-Aswad bin Amr informed us, saying: I am Ibn Wahb. He said: Hafs bin Maysarah informed me, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba. On the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Marwan, on the authority of his father, that Ka’b swore to him by God who parted the sea for Moses: We find in the Torah that David When the Prophet of God finished his prayer, he would say: “O God, make right for me my religion which You have made for me a protection, and make right for me my world in which You have made My livelihood, O God, I seek refuge in Your satisfaction from Your wrath, and I seek refuge, meaning, in Your forgiveness from Your vengeance, and I seek refuge in You from You, there is no objection to what You have given “And there is no one who will give what you withhold, and the hardworking will not benefit from you.” He said: Ka’b told me that Suhayb told him that Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He used to say them when he finished his prayer. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1252","Amr ibn Ali, narrated by Yahya, informed us on the authority of Uthman al-Shahham, on the authority of Muslim ibn Abi Bakra, who said: My father used to say after the prayer: “O God I seek refuge in You from disbelief, poverty, and the torment of the grave.” So I was saying them, and my father said: From whom did you take this? I said: On your authority. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say them after the prayer."
"1253","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are two characteristics that a Muslim man will not count unless he enters Paradise. They are easy, and whoever does them are few,” he said. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The five daily prayers, one of you glorifies God ten after each prayer, praises ten, and glorifies God.” “Ten, it is one hundred and fifty on the tongue, and one thousand and five hundred on the scale.” I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, concluding them. With his hand, “So when one of you goes to his bed or resting place, he says Subhani thirty-three times, and “Thanks” thirty-three times, and he says “Allahu Akbar” thirty-four times. It is a hundred on the tongue and a thousand in the scale.” He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Which of you works every day and night?” For two thousand and five hundred bad deeds? It was said: O Messenger of God, how can he not count them? He said: “The devil comes to one of you while he is praying and says: Remember such-and-such, remember such-and-such, and he comes to him when he is sleeping and makes him sleep.”"
"1254","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Samra told us, on the authority of Asbat, Amr bin Qais told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, On the authority of Ka’b bin Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They are things that are repeated and the one who says them will not be disappointed. He glorifies God three times after every prayer.” thirty, and He praises Him thirty-three times, and He glorifies Him thirty-four times,” and on the authority of Mahmoud bin Ghaylan, on the authority of Qubaysah, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour On the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1255","Musa bin Hazzam al-Tirmidhi told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Ibn Idris, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin On the authority of Kathir ibn Aflah, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: They were commanded to say “Tasbih” thirty-three times after every prayer, and “thank God” thirty-three times. And they say “Allahu Akbar” thirty-four times. Then a man from the Ansar came in his dream and it was said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded you to say “Tasbih” at the end of every day. Prayer thirty-three times, and praise be to God thirty-three times, and say “Allahu Akbar” thirty-four times? He said: Yes. He said: So make it twenty-five, and put the Tahlil in it. When morning came, he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned That was for him, so he said: “Make it that way.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1256","Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah al-Karim Abu Zar’ah al-Razi told us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Yunus told us, he said: Ali ibn al-Fadil told me. Ibn Iyad, on the authority of Abdul Aziz Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that a man from the Ansar saw what a sleeper sees, he was told : What did your Prophet command you to do? He said: “We are commanded to glorify God thirty-three times, and to praise God thirty-three times, and to glorify God thirty-four times, so that is one hundred.” He said: “Glorify God five times.” And twenty, and they say thank you twenty-five, and they say “Allahu Akbar” twenty-five, and they say “Hallah” twenty-five, so that’s a hundred.” So when the morning came, he mentioned that. To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do as the Ansari said.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1257","Muhammad bin Bashar, na Muhammad na Shu`bah, informed us on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, the client of the family of Talha, who said: I heard Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by her while she was in the mosque praying and supplicating, then he passed by her close to Midday, so he said to her: “Are you still doing that?” She said: Yes. He said: “Shall I not teach you?” meaning “words that you say.” Glory be to God, the number of His creation. Glory be to God according to the number of His creation, Glory be to God the number of His creation, Glory be to God His satisfaction, Glory be to God His satisfaction, Glory be to God His satisfaction Himself, Glory be to God, the weight of His throne, Glory be to God, the weight of His throne, Glory be to God, the weight of His throne, Glory be to God, the ink of His words, Glory be to God The ink of His words, Glory be to God, the ink of His words.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1258","Ali bin Hajar told us, I am Attab, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Ikrimah, and Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The poor came to the Prophet and he prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. They said: O Messenger of God, the rich pray as we pray, and fast as we fast, and they have wealth that they give in charity. And they are freed. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you pray, say: Glory be to God thirty-three, and praise be to God thirty-three.” “And God is the Greatest, thirty-four times, and there is no god but God, ten times. Thus, you will overtake those who came before you, and you will precede those after you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1259","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told me, he said: My father told me, Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Abu Alqamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says the Sublime at the end of every prayer In the morning, say a hundred times of tasbihah, and say a hundred times of Allah, his sins will be forgiven, even if they are like the foam of the sea.”"
"1260","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani and al-Hussein ibn Muhammad al-Dhari’ informed us, and the pronunciation for it, he said: Utham ibn Ali told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, On the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, praising God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1261","Qutaibah told us, he said: Bakr, who is Ibn Mudar, told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Haad, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah ibn Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to be generous during the ten days in the middle of the month. When twenty nights have passed and he arrives the twenty-one, he will return to his dwelling, and those who were with him will return. Then he stayed in A month ago, it was the same night that he was returning, so he addressed the people and ordered them to do as God wished. Then he said: “I was being friendly.” These ten days, then it seemed to me that I would adhere to these last ten days, so whoever was in seclusion with me, let him remain in his seclusion, and I saw This night, I forgot about it, so seek it during the last ten days of every odd night, and you saw me prostrating in water and mud.” Abu Sa’id said. Al-Khudri: It rained on the night of the twenty-first, and it stopped raining on the mosque in the prayer area of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I looked at him as he had left. morning prayer, his face wet with mud and water (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1262","Qutaibah told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If He prayed Fajr and sat in his place of prayer until the sun rose.”"
"1263","Ahmad bin Sulaiman, narrated to us by Yahya bin Adam, narrated by Zuhayr, and another mentioned, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, said: I said to Jabir bin Samurah: Were you sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he prayed the dawn prayer, he would sit in his place of prayer until the sun rose, and his companions would talk.” They mention the hadith of pre-Islamic times, they sing poetry, they laugh, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, smiles.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1264","Qutaibah, narrated to us by Abu Awanah, told us on the authority of Al-Suddi, he said: I asked Anas bin Malik: “How do I turn away when I pray? To my right, or to my right.” My left? He said: As for me, most of the time I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turning to his right."
"1265","Abu Hafs Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: Abdullah said: “Do not let any of you Satan has a part of himself. He believes that it is his right not to turn away except to his right. I have seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, more \His turning to his left\"""""""
"1266","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, I am Baqiya bin Al-Walid, he said: Al-Zubaidi told us, that Makhul narrated to him, that Masruq bin Al-Ajda’ narrated to him On the authority of Aisha, she said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, drinking while standing and sitting, praying barefoot and wearing shoes, and turning away from on his right and on his left.”"
"1267","Ali bin Khashram told us, he said: I am Jesus, he is Ibn Yunus, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ The women used to pray with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, at dawn, and when he said the salaam, they would leave, covering themselves with their loincloths, so that they would not be known who had been dishonest.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1268","Ali bin Hajar, I am Ali bin Mushar, told us on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Fulfil, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer. One day, peace be upon him, then he turned to us with his face and said: “As for me, I am your imam, so do not hasten to kneel, prostrate, or prostrate.” By standing, or by leaving, for I see you in front of me and behind me.” Then he said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if you saw what I saw, You would have laughed a little, and you would have cried a lot. We said: What did you see, O Messenger of God? He said: “Paradise and Hell.”"
"1269","Ismail bin Masoud, from Bishr, and he is Ibn al-Mufaddal, told us, he said: Dawud, who is Ibn Abi Hind, told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abd. Al-Rahman, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Abu Dharr, said: We fasted Ramadan with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not lead us in the prayer. peace be upon him, until there were seven days of the month left, so he stayed with us until about a third of the night had passed, then it was the sixth day, and he did not get up, so when It was five o'clock. He led us until about halfway through the night. I said: O Messenger of God, if you would spare us the opportunity to pray this night, he said: “When a man prays with the imam until he leaves, it is counted for him that he has spent a night in prayer.” He said: Then it was the fourth time and he did not stand with us, so when three of the prayers remained During the month, he sent for his daughters and wives, and mobilized the people. He led us so much that we feared that the farmer would miss us, then he did not support us for any of the month. He said: Daoud: I said: What is Al-Falah? He said: Suhoor (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1270","Ahmad bin Bakkar Al-Harrani told me, on the authority of Bishr bin Al-Sari, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed bin Abi Hussein Al-Nawfali, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, On the authority of Uqba bin Al-Harith, he said: I prayed the afternoon prayer with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in Medina, then he left, quickly stepping over people’s necks, until The people were amazed at his speed, so some of his companions followed him, and he went in to see some of his wives, then he left, then he said: “I mentioned it while I was in the afternoon prayer.” We had some wheat, but I did not like it to spend the night with us, so I ordered it to be divided.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1271","Ismail bin Masoud and Muhammad bin Abd al-Ala informed us, saying: Khalid, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that Omar bin Al Khattab, on the day of the ditch after the sun had set, started cursing The infidels of Quraysh, and he said: O Messenger of God, I had hardly begun to pray until the sun was about to set, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By God When I prayed it, we went down with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Batha. He performed ablution for the prayer, and we performed ablution for it, so he prayed the afternoon prayer after The sun has set, then pray Maghrib after that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1272","I am Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem Al-Anbari, he said: I am Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Asma, he said: I am Juwayriyah bin Asma, on the authority of Al-Walid Ibn Abi Hisham, on the authority of Nafi’, that Abdullah Ibn Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Pray in your homes, and do not You will take them as graves.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1273","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Tamim Al-Masisi told me, he said: I heard Hajjaj, he said: Ibn Juraij said, Musa bin Uqba told me, On the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best prayer is the prayer of a person in his home, except for the prayer \the written\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1274","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Affan bin Muslim told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: I heard Musa bin Uqba, he said: I heard Abu al-Nadr. He narrates, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Pray, O people, in your homes, for “The best prayer for a person is in his home, except for the obligatory prayers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1275","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Nadr, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, that Zayd bin Thabit said: “The best prayer is “Your prayer is in your homes, that is, except for congregational prayer.”"
"1276","Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, he said: Yahya, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, he said: I said, O Mother of the Believers, inform me about the rising of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: Do you not recite this Surah? Al-Muzzammil? I said: Yes, she said: “For God assumed the night prayer at the beginning of this Surah, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions stood up for about Until their feet swelled, and God withheld its end for twelve months, then God sent down the mitigation at the end of this Surah, so it became The voluntary night prayer after an obligatory prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1277","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever prays Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, all his previous sins will be forgiven.”"
"1278","Muhammad bin Ismail al-Tabarani told us, he said: Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Asma’ told us, he said: Juwayriyah na, on the authority of Malik, he said: na Al-Zuhri said: Abu Salama bin Abdul-Rahman and Humaid bin Abdul-Rahman told me on the authority of Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever observes Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1279","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, In the mosque one night, people led his prayer, then he prayed from the midwife, and the people increased, then they gathered on the third or fourth night. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not go out to them. When morning came, he said: “I saw what you did, but nothing prevented me from going out to you.” However, I feared that it would be imposed on you, and that was during Ramadan."
"1280","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id Abu Qudamah al-Sarkhasi told me, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl told me, on the authority of Dawud, who is Ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of al-Walid Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Dharr, said: We fasted with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, during Ramadan, but he did not stand up for us until he remained Seven days of the month, so he stayed with us until a third of the night had passed, then he did not lead us in prayer at the sixth, so he stayed with us at the fifth, until half of the night had passed. night, so I said: O Messenger of God, if we escape for the rest of this night, he said: “Whoever stands with the Imam until he leaves, it will be recorded for him “Then he did not lead us in prayer until three days of the month remained, so he joined us on the third day, and gathered his family and wives until we were afraid that We miss the farmer. I said: What is the farmer? He said: Suhoor (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1281","Ahmad bin Sulaiman, Abdah bin Abdullah, and Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid told us, and the pronunciation is for Ahmad. He said: Zayd bin Hubab. He said: Muawiyah bin Saleh told me, he said: Nu’aym bin Ziyad Abu Talha told me, he said: I heard Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, on the pulpit of Homs, He says: “We stood with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the month of Ramadan, on the night of the twenty-third until the first third of the night, then we rose with him.” On the night of the twenty-fifth until midnight, then we rose on the night of the twenty-nine until we thought that we would not reach Al-Falah, and they called it suhoor.”"
"1282","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Our Yahya is Ibn Sa’id al-Qattan, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, he said: Al-Qaqa’ told me, on the authority of my father Saleh, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God have mercy on a man who got up during the night and prayed, then woke up his wife.” Then she prayed, but if she refused, he sprinkled water on her face, and may God have mercy on a woman who got up during the night and prayed, then woke up her husband, and he prayed. If he refuses, I will sprinkle water on his face.”"
"1283","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “When one of you sleeps, Satan will tie three knots on his head, striking each knot for a long night, meaning: Lie down, and when he wakes up and remembers God, one knot is untied, then he performs ablution, another is untied, and if he prays, all the knots are untied, and in the morning He has a good soul and is active, otherwise he becomes evil and sluggish.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1284","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He was mentioned with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. A man slept one night until the morning. He said: “That is a man in whose ears Satan urinated.”"
"1285","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Ours is Abdullah, and he is Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Do not be like so-and-so. He used to pray at night, so he abandoned The night prayer.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Bishr ibn Bakr entered between Yahya and Abu Salamah, Omar ibn al-Hakam."
"1286","Al-Harith bin Asad told us, he said: Bishr bin Bakr told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told me, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, on the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Hakam Ibn Thuban, he said: Abu Salamah told me, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Abdullah, do not be like so-and-so who used to pray the night prayers, but then he abandoned the night prayers.”"
"1287","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid told me that Shurayh Al-Hadrami, was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “That is a man who does not recite the Qur’an.”"
"1288","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ismail told us, and Imran bin Musa told us, on the authority of Abdul-Warith, on the authority of Abdul-Aziz, On the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque with a rope stretched between two poles, and he said: “What is this?” They said: Zainab. If she is listless or lazy, she becomes attached to him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let one of you carry out his activity. If he is lazy or lethargic, let him sit.”"
"1289","Shuaib bin Yusuf told me, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered She has a woman with her, so he said: “Who is this?” She said: So-and-so does not sleep and remembers her prayers. So he said: “Meh, do as much as you can. By God, God does not get bored until you get bored, but the most beloved to Him is the religion as long as it is its owner.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1290","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Our is Ishaq, and he is the son of Yusuf al-Azraq, on the authority of Awf Al-A’rabi, on the authority of Abu Khaled, and his name is I have: An immigrant, Abu Mukhlid says, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, he said: Abu Muslim told me, he said: I said to Abu Dharr: Which night prayer is better? He said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “It is midnight and the doer of it is few.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1291","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yahya told us, and he is the son of Adam, he said: Zuhair told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I came Al-Aswad bin Yazid, who was a brother and friend of mine, so I said: O Abu Amr, tell me what the Mother of the Believers told you about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: She said: “He used to sleep at the beginning of the night, and wake up at the end of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1292","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar, a Kufi, informed us, saying: Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Musa, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar On the authority of Al-Aghar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id and Abu Hurairah, they said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever wakes up during the night and wakes up his wife So they prayed two rak'ahs together, destined for men and women who often remember God.”"
"1293","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hussein, that Al-Hussein bin Ali told him, On the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went to him and Fatima, and said: “Aren’t you praying?” I said: O Messenger of God, it is only ourselves. In the hand of God, if He wishes to send us, He will send us, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, departed while I told him that, then I heard him saying A plotter strikes his thigh and says: Man was the most argumentative. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1294","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best fasting after the month of Ramadan is the month of God, Muharram, and the best prayer after the obligatory prayer is “Night.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Shu’bah sent him."
"1295","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, that he heard Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best prayer after the obligatory prayer is the night prayer, and the best fasting after Ramadan Muharram.”"
"1296","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I heard a quarterly report, on the authority of Zayd ibn Dhabyan, He transmitted it to Abu Dharr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “There are three whom God loves: A man who came to a people and asked them about God, but he did not He asked them because of his kinship with them, but they prevented him, so a man lagged behind them, so he gave him a secret. No one knows his gift except God, who He gave it to him, and some people walked throughout the night until sleep was more beloved to them than what they had to do with it. They came down and lowered their heads, and he stood up and flattered me. And he recites My verses, and a man was in a expedition, and they met the enemy and were defeated, so he attacked him until he was killed, or a victory was opened for him.” Sufyan disagreed with him. Al-Thawri, Muhammad bin Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqqi told me, he said: Muhammad bin Ali bin Maimun Al-Ruqi told me, he said: Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faryabi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rabi’i, on the authority of Abu Dharr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said something similar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1297","Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Sadran, Basri, told us on the authority of Bishr, who is Ibn al-Mufaddal. He said: Shu’bah, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Sulaym, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Masruq, he said: I said to Aisha: Which work is most beloved to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: Always. I said: What night did he rise in the night? She said: If he hears the one screaming (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1298","Isma bin Al-Fadl, a Nisaburi, told us, he said: Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, he said: Al-Azhar told me that he is the son of Saeed, on the authority of Asim bin Humaid, who said: I asked Aisha: How did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, begin the night prayers? She said: You asked me about something that no one had asked me about before you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say “Allahu Akbar” ten times, and praise Ten times, and he glorifies God ten times, and says God ten times, and asks forgiveness ten times, and says: “O God, forgive me, guide me, provide for me, and protect me, I seek refuge in By God, from the narrow situation on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"1299","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Muammar, and Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Rabi’a bin Ka’b Al-Aslami said: I used to spend the night at the room of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I used to hear him when he got up at night, saying: “Glory be to God, Lord of the worlds” Al-Hawai, then he says: “Glory be to God and praise be to Him” Al-Hawai (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1300","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Ahwal, meaning Suleiman bin Abi Muslim, Makki, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up at night, he would recite the supplication of God’s prayers, saying: “O God, praise be to You, You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and whoever is in them. To You belongs all praise, You are the supremacy of the heavens and the earth and all that is in them, and to You belongs all praise, You are the Sovereign of the heavens and the earth and all that is in them, and to You belongs all praise, for You are the Truth. Your promise is true, and Paradise is true, and Hell is true, and the Hour is true, and the prophets are true, and Muhammad is true, to you I have submitted, and in you I have put my trust, And in You I have believed.” And he mentioned a word that means: “And by You I disputed, and to You I judged. Forgive me what I have put forward, and what I have delayed, and what I have concealed and what I have declared.” You are the advance, and you are the latter. There is no god but You, and there is no power nor strength except in God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1301","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Humaid bin Abdul Rahman bin told me Auf, that a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I said: I was on a journey with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: By God I would go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for prayer; Until I saw what he did, “When he prayed the evening prayer, which was dark, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lay down in the dark during the night, and then He woke up, looked at the horizon, and said: Our Lord, You did not create this void until it reached that you do not break your promise. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, tempted He went to his bed with his hand, took out a siwak from it, then emptied water into a cup from a container he had, so he cleaned himself, then got up and prayed. Until I said: He had prayed as much as he had slept, then he lay down until I said: He had slept as much as he had prayed, then he woke up and did as he did the first time, and said: Just like that. He said, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did so three times before dawn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1302","Amr bin Ali informed us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, al-A’mash, and Husayn, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Hudhayfah, The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When he got up at night, he would cover his mouth with the siwak.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1303","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem Al-Anbari told us, he said: Omar bin Yunus told us, he said: Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi told us Many, he said: Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: I asked Aisha: With what did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, begin the prayer? She said: When he got up at night, he would begin his prayer: “O God, Lord of Gabriel, Michael, and Israfil, Creator of the heavens and the earth, All-Knowing The unseen and the witnessed, You judge between Your servants in that in which they differed, O God, guide me to the truth in that in which they differed. Indeed, You guide those who You desire a straight path.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1304","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Yazid, he said: I am Praiseworthy, on the authority of Anas, he said: “We did not want to see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he prayed the salaam at night unless we saw him, and we did not want to see him sleeping unless we saw him.”"
"1305","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Hajjaj told me, he said: Ibn Jurayj said, on the authority of his father, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaika told me, that Ya’la bin Mamlik told him that he asked Umm Salamah about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: “He used to pray the dark prayer, then He recites the tasbih, then prays after that for as long as God wills during the night, then he goes out and lies down as he prayed, then he wakes up from that sleep. Then he will pray as he slept, and his prayer of the afterlife will last until dawn.”"
"1306","Qutayba bin Saeed and Muhammad bin Mansour told us, and the wording is his, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, he said: I heard Al-Mughirah Ibn Shu'bah says: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood until his feet swelled, and he was told: God has forgiven you of your previous sins and what He delayed and said: “Shall I not be a grateful servant?” ! (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1307","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Saleh bin Mahran told me, he said: Al-Numan bin Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to pray until his feet slipped.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1308","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Amr bin Aws, that he heard Abdullah bin Amr Ibn Al-Aas says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The most beloved of God’s fasts is the fasting of David. He used to fast one day and break his fast the next. The most beloved prayer to God is the prayer of David. He used to sleep at midnight, a third of it he would wake up, and a sixth of it he would sleep.”"
"1309","Muhammad bin Ali bin Harb Al-Maruzi informed us, saying: Muadh bin Khalid informed us, saying: Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, On the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I came on the night of my journey to Moses by the Red Dune, and he was He is standing and praying in his grave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1310","Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Rabbati told me, he said: Habban told us, he said: Hammad told us, and he is Ibn Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, and Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Anas The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I passed by Moses while he was praying in his grave.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is more likely to be correct. From those before him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1311","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir told us, he said: I heard my father, he said: I heard Anas, saying: Some of the companions of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “On the night of his captivity, he passed by Moses while he was praying in his grave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1312","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adiy, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of some of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “On the night of my journey, I passed by Moses while he was praying in his grave.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1313","Amr bin Othman bin Saeed told me, he said: My father told me, and the rest of them, they said: Ibn Abi Hamza told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, he said: Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Nawfal told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Khabab bin Al-Art, on the authority of his father, and he had witnessed Full moon with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: He watched the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a night in which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. And he greeted all of them until it was dawn, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished his prayer, a preacher came to him and said: O Messenger of God, By my father and mother, you prayed tonight a prayer that I have never seen you pray like. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Yes, it is a prayer.” Desire and fear, I asked my Lord about three qualities, and He gave me two, and withheld one from me: I asked my Lord not to destroy us with what He destroyed us with. The nations came before us, so He gave them to me, and I asked my Lord not to make us an enemy of others, so He gave them to me, and I asked my Lord not to divide us into sects. So he prevented her.”"
"1314","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Nawfal informed me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Khabab bin Al-Art, that Khabab said: I looked The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in a prayer that he prayed until it was dawn. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him from his prayer, a baker came. He said: O Messenger of God, may my mother and father be sacrificed for you, I prayed a prayer tonight! He said: Yes, it is a prayer of desire and dread. I asked my Lord about three qualities, and He gave me two, and withheld one from me. I asked Him not to He will destroy us with what He destroyed the nations before us. So he gave it to me, and I asked him not to make anyone other than us an enemy. So he gave it to me, and I asked him. That He does not confuse us with sects, so He prevented us from doing so.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1315","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid al-Muqri informed us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Yafour, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, he said: She said: Aisha: “When the ten days of prayer came, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, revived the night, woke up his family, and tightened the apron.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1316","Harun ibn Ishaq al-Hamdani al-Kufi informed us, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, on the authority of Sa`d Ibn Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I do not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited the entire Qur’an in one night, nor did he stand up until the morning.” “And he did not fast an entire month other than Ramadan.”"
"1317","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of his father, that Abdullah bin Qais bin Makhramah He told him, on the authority of Zaid bin Khaled Al-Juhani, that he said: “To improve the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he prayed two light rak’ahs. Then he prayed two long, long rak'ahs, then he prayed two rak'ahs, which were inferior to the ones before them, then he prayed two rak'ahs, which were less than the two before them, then he prayed two rak'ahs, and they were less than the two before them, then he prayed two rak'ahs, and they were less than the two before them, then If you pray Witr, that is thirteen rak’ahs.”"
"1318","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Makhramah bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Kurayb, that Ibn Abbas told him that he spent the night At the house of Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she was his paternal aunt. He said: So I lay down on the width of the pillow, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lay down. peace be upon him and his family throughout its duration, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slept until midnight, or a little before it, or Shortly after that, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up. He sat and wiped the sleep from his face with his hand, then he recited the ten verses. The rings from Surah Al Imran. Then he got up to a hanging pen, and performed ablution from it. He performed his ablution well, then he stood up to pray. Ibn Abbas said: So I got up and did the same as he did, then I went and stood beside him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed his right hand on my head, and he took my right ear and twisted it, so he prayed two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs Then he prayed the Witr prayer, then he lay down until the muezzin came to him, so he got up and prayed two light rak’ahs, then he went out for the morning prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1319","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Makhramah bin Sulaiman, that Kurayb, the client of Ibn Abbas, told him, saying: I asked Ibn Abbas, I said: How was the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? Peace be upon him at night? He said: “He was reciting in one of his rooms, and the person behind him could hear his recitation, and he said: He spent the night with him while he was with Maimuna bint Al-Harith, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Maimunah lay down on a pillow of human hair stuffed with fibres, and he slept until a third of the time had passed. During the night or half of it, he woke up and got up to a container with water in it, so he performed ablution, and I performed ablution with him, then he got up, and I stood next to him on his left. So he placed me on his right, and he placed his hand on my head and began to wipe my ears as if he were waking me up, so he prayed two light rak’ahs, in which I said: He recited Umm al-Qur’an in every rak’ah, then he said the salaam, then he prayed two rak’ahs, then he prayed the salaam, until he prayed eleven rak’ahs with Witr, then he slept until He became heavy, and I saw him breathing, so Bilal came to him and said: Prayer, O Messenger of God, so he stood up and prayed two rak’ahs, and he prayed for the people, but he did not perform ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1320","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Samra Al-Ahmasi, a Kufi, told us: Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Then my father sent me to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with camels that he gave him as charity camels. When he came to him, and it was the night of Maimuna, and Maimuna was the maternal aunt of Ibn Abbas. He came to the mosque and prayed the evening prayer. Then he came and threw off his garment, then entered with His wife was in her clothes, so I took my dress and began to fold it under me, then I lay on it, then I said: I will not sleep tonight until I see... To what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, does. So he slept until he blew, until part of the night had passed as God wished for it to go, then he got up. So he went out and urinated, then he came to a water-bearer who was brought to him, and he untied him, then he poured water on his hands, then he stepped on the water-bearer’s mouth, and he began to wash himself. His hands, then he performed ablution until he finished, and I wanted to get up, so I poured water on him, so I was afraid that he would leave the night for my sake. Then he got up to pray, so I got up. So I did the same as he did, then I came to him and stood to his left, so he took me in his hand and placed me on his right. He prayed thirteen rak’ahs. Then he lay down until Bilal came to him and called for prayer, so he got up and prayed two rak’ahs before dawn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
